# Living docs (mandatory)

Every meaningful code/config change **must** update documentation in the **same turn** — not later.

## Always update

1. **`CHANGELOG.md`** under `[Unreleased]` (Keep a Changelog: Added / Changed / Fixed / Removed). One clear bullet per user-visible or architectural change.
2. **`docs/current-state.md`** — status table + “Next” + `Last updated` date.
3. **`specs/<feature>/tasks.md`** — check off completed tasks / note partial progress.
4. **`docs/scorecard.md`** — when the change moves rubric evidence (API, tests, deploy, onboarding wiring, hex/ROP). Re-score with **strict hiring-bar** protocol (§0); never inflate.

## Update when relevant

| If you change… | Also update… |
|---|---|
| HTTP routes / DTOs | `docs/api/openapi.json` (+ Postman if used) |
| Architecture decision | new/updated `docs/adr/00xx-*.md` + `AGENTS.md` if fixed rules change |
| How to run / env / stack | `README.md`, `.env.example` |
| Cursor conventions | `.cursor/rules/*` (and mention in CHANGELOG if agent-facing) |

## Do not

- Ship code-only diffs while leaving CHANGELOG/current-state stale.
- Write vague changelog lines (“misc”, “updates”); say **what** changed and **why** it matters.
- Put secrets or the payment company brand in public docs.

## Definition of done (every task)

Code + tests (as required) + CHANGELOG + current-state + tasks.md (+ OpenAPI/ADR/README if touched).
